From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:40:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 017/342] usb: add DWC2 host controller driver for the Amlogic
 Meson GXBB

Synopsys DesignWare DWC2 (DWC_otg 3.10a on the S905/ODROID-C2) in host
mode with buffer DMA, attached through the device tree
("amlogic,meson-gxbb-usb"), loaded as a boot module:

- platform bring-up the firmware does not do when booting over the
  network: clock gates, USB reset, VBUS (GPIOAO_5) and the onboard hub's
  reset (GPIOAO_4, read-modify-write so GPIOAO_3, the SD card's I/O
  voltage, is untouched), PHY power-on reset with the 24 MHz reference
- core reset, forced host mode, 16-bit UTMI+, FIFO sizing, then the
  interrupt handler is installed with everything masked except channel
  halts
- emulated one-port root hub mapped onto HPRT (written from a masked copy
  so its write-1-to-clear bits are not hit)
- a worker thread runs transfers one at a time on channel 0 through a
  64 KB bounce buffer with cache maintenance: control transfers stage by
  stage, bulk in one go, interrupt IN retried every 10 ms on NAK
- split transactions (low/full speed devices behind a high speed hub) are
  not implemented yet and refused with B_NOT_SUPPORTED

Tested on the ODROID-C2: the GL852G hub is enumerated
(listusb: 05e3:0610 "Genesys Logic, Inc." "Hub").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
