+/*
+ * Copyright 2026, haiku-odroid-c2 port authors.
+ * Distributed under the terms of the MIT License.
+ *
+ * Synopsys DesignWare "DWC2" (DWC_otg) USB 2.0 controller in host mode, as
+ * the host port of the Amlogic Meson GXBB (S905, ODROID-C2).
+ *
+ * Programming model after FreeBSD's dwc_otg.c (BSD-2-Clause) and Plan 9's
+ * usbdwc.c (MIT); the GXBB PHY, clock gate, reset and GPIO details after
+ * NetBSD's meson_usbphy.c and friends (BSD-2-Clause). No code was taken from
+ * them. Design notes: docs/m5-usb-dwc2-design.md in the port's repository.
+ *
+ * This first version:
+ * - brings up the platform itself (U-Boot does not touch USB when booting
+ *   over the network): clock gates, reset, VBUS, PHY, hub reset;
+ * - uses buffer DMA through one bounce buffer with explicit cache
+ *   maintenance (the DMA does not snoop the CPU caches);
+ * - runs transfers one at a time on host channel 0 from a worker thread:
+ *   control transfers stage by stage, bulk in one go, interrupt IN as one
+ *   attempt that is retried every 10 ms while the device NAKs;
+ * - does not do split transactions yet, so low/full speed devices behind a
+ *   high speed hub (keyboards and mice behind the ODROID-C2's GL852G hub)
+ *   are refused with B_NOT_SUPPORTED.
+ */
+
